          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TFT"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            (necessarily flat) which is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with coefficients in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          %p
            Viewed in a broader context and generalizing: Dijkgraaf-Witten theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            induced from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G := Disc B G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            here is an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            this is traditional Dijkgraaf-Witten theory, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            and the background field is a circle 4-bundle, then this is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yetter+model"} Yetter model
          %p
            This are the first two steps in filtering of target spaces by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory#DiscreteTargets"} with discrete target spaces
          %h3#concise_survey_of_the_ingredients Concise survey of the ingredients
          %p
