            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-k}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} (k-1)-category
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p …
          %h2#relation_to_chernsimons_theory Relation to Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Dijkgraaf-Witten theory is to be thought of as the finite group version of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Lie ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+in+group+cohomology"} transgression in group cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 1d Chern-Simons theory
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1d+Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} 1d Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 3d Chern-Simons theory
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %strong Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} 2d Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 4d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 6d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} infinite-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-model"} AKSZ sigma-model
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#DijkgraafWitten90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robbert+Dijkgraaf"}> Robbert Dijkgraaf
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Gauge Theories and Group Cohomology
              %strong 129
              (1990) 393 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02096988"}> doi:10.1007/BF02096988
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-129/issue-2/Topological-gauge-theories-and-group-cohomology/cmp/1104180750.full"} euclid:cmp/1104180750
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/files/DW.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-Hopf+algebra"} quasi-Hopf algebra
            associated with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \colon \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
            originates in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robbert+Dijkgraaf"}> Robbert Dijkgraaf
              , V. Pasquier, P. Roche,
              = succeed "," do
                %em QuasiHopf algebras, group cohomology and orbifold models
              %strong 18B
              (1990), 60-72;
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quasi-quantum groups related to orbifold models
          %p A review is in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Coste, J-M. Maillard,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representation Theory of Twisted Group Double
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0309257"} arXiv:hep-th/0309257
          %p and conceptual clarifications were established in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Willerton"}> Simon Willerton
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The twisted Drinfeld double of a finite group via gerbes and finite groupoids
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0503266"} arXiv/math.QA/0503266
          %p
            and, earlier, in an unpublished manuscript of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Bressler"} Paul Bressler
            (2002-2004). See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Drinfeld+double"} Drinfeld double
            for more on this.
          %p
            A first comprehensive structural account of DW theory as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} functorial QFT
            was given in
          %ul#FreedQuinn93
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Quinn"} Frank Quinn
              %em Chern-Simons theory with finite gauge group
              Commun.Math.Phys.
              = succeed ":435-472," do
                %strong 156
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://de.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9111004"} arXiv:hep-th/9111004
          %p A review is given on p. 68 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"}> Bruce Bartlett
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical aspects of topological quantum field theory
              %a{:href => "http://de.arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0512103"} arXiv/math.QA/0512103
          %p
            First steps towards understand DW theory as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            appear in
          %ul#Freed94
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              %em Higher Algebraic Structures and Quantization
              Commun.Math.Phys. 159 (1994) 343-398 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:hep-th/9212115"}> arXiv:arXiv:hep-th/9212115
              )
          %p
            Discussion aiming towards a refinement of DW theory to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Kevin Wray,
              %em Extended topological gauge theories in codimension 0 and higher
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~kwray/papers/thesis.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Further conceptual refinement of this is indicated in section 3 and section 8 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
              (2010)
          %p
            This proposes a general abstract way to construct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            quantizations for finite group theories such as DW, see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Finiteness and ambidexterity in
                  = succeed "-local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(n)
              %em Notre Dame Graduate Summer School on Topology and Field Theories
              and
              %em Harvard lecture
              2012 (
